# Legacy .html URLs from the pre-restructure site. These paths no longer
# correspond to real files (content now lives under clean-URL directories),
# so without an explicit rule Cloudflare Pages was falling back to serving
# the homepage's index.html at each of these URLs — with its canonical tag
# pointing back to the homepage. That created duplicate-content pages at
# stale URLs. 301 them straight to the correct current page instead.
/whats-included.html   /whats-included/   301
/pricing.html           /pricing/           301
/landing-pages.html     /landing-pages/     301
/about.html             /about/             301
/faq.html               /faq/               301
/guides.html            /guides/            301
